<title>RUSSIA: Russia 113-day T-bill yields avg 19.71 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia 113-day T-bill yields avg 19.71 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised yield on an additional 113-day tranche of GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22082) was 19.71 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the average yield at 20.62 percent to 20.85 percent.</p>
<p>The original issue closed on Tuesday at 92.86 to yield 20.94 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>    Series number		     22082</p>
<p>    Issue volume			4.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		     1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		    7.26 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)			 6.73 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold				  4.46 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			    4.16 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price		     93.30 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	   93.30 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		     19.71 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	  19.71 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)		 133 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		     Oct 15, 1997</p>
<p>    Original issue date	     May 7, 1997</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry raised 6.09 trillion roubles in an earlier sale of series 21073 266-day bills, bringing the total proceeds from Wednesday's auctions to 10.25 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry also repaid about 8.92 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 238-day T-bills (series 23053).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
